//  anima-eeg-core/tool/modules/_metrics/phi_proxy_native.hexa  (Phase 5e)
//
//  PURPOSE
//    Pure-native PORT of the sample-partition Φ★ canonical metric (the
//    1순위 5-method ⭐ ranked TOP-1 in `docs/p9_paradigm_b_eeg_phi_proxy_2026_05_03.md`
//    §1.3 + §1.6 comparison table) — same-formula-different-substrate port
//    of `tool/anima_phi_v3_canonical.hexa` (Mistral-7B hidden state, baseline
//    +41.86 from `.roadmap.eeg:10` cross-substrate ledger entry) onto the
//    EEG channel substrate.
//
//    Resolves blocker `eeg.blk.4`:  EEG-derived φ proxy spec FROZEN +
//    sample-partition φ on EEG (5th ⭐ candidate) port — moves cond.4 status
//    from "spec only" toward "IMPL" status_emit `__EEG_PHI_PROXY__ <SPEC|IMPL|CROSS_VALIDATED>`.
//
//  SPEC SOURCE (cite chain — raw#15 SSOT, no invention)
//    [S1] `.roadmap.eeg:10` (entry id eeg.phi_proxy.cross_substrate_plan):
//         "anima_phi_v3_canonical baseline 41.86 (CLM hidden state) ↔ EEG
//          sample-partition φ proxy (5th ⭐ candidate same-formula-different-substrate)"
//    [S2] `docs/p9_paradigm_b_eeg_phi_proxy_2026_05_03.md` §1.3 (line 54-60):
//         "window EEG → matrix X ∈ R^{N_samples × C} → top-variance HID =
//          max(2, N//2) → I_full = log|Cov(X_t)| → K random sample
//          partitions → I_1 + I_2 → φ_k = I_full − (I_1 + I_2) → MIN over K"
//    [S3] `tool/anima_phi_v3_canonical.hexa` (canonical CLM impl, frozen):
//         AUTO-CONDITIONING HID_TRUNC = max(2, N//2) — well-conditioned
//         regime, both full + half covariances full-rank.
//    [S4] `docs/n_substrate_consciousness_roadmap_2026_05_01.md:1297`:
//         "CLM v4 530M = +41.86 ⭐ unique-positive (8× Llama, 40× Qwen3)"
//    [S5] `docs/p9_paradigm_b_eeg_phi_proxy_2026_05_03.md:205`:
//         "δ enforces Φ★(model_hidden) ≥ 5.0 (8× safety margin vs baseline 41.86)"
//
//  ALGORITHM (frozen-spec port, no invention)
//    1. Window EEG → X ∈ R^{N × C} where N = sample count, C = channel count.
//       For 16ch hardware C=16; native selftest fixture uses N=64, C=16 to
//       match auto-cond regime (HID = max(2, N//2) clamped to C).
//    2. Per-channel mean-center: X_c = X - mean(X, axis=0).
//    3. Top-variance HID truncation:
//          HID_TRUNC = min(C, max(2, N // 2))
//          Pick top-HID channels by per-channel variance.
//          (For 16ch hardware, N=16 → HID=8 — well-conditioned; for N >> C,
//           HID stays at C.)
//    4. I_full = log |Cov(X_t)| where Cov is HID×HID empirical with ridge
//       regularisation (1e-3 ULP) for numerical stability.
//    5. K random sample-partitions (FNV-deterministic seed=42 RNG):
//          For each k ∈ [0..K):
//             perm = FNV permutation of N row indices
//             S1 = perm[0:HALF], S2 = perm[HALF:N], HALF = N // 2
//             I_1 = log |Cov(X_t[S1])|     (HID×HID, HALF samples)
//             I_2 = log |Cov(X_t[S2])|
//             φ_k = I_full − (I_1 + I_2)
//          Φ★_min = MIN over K (canonical strict, matches anima_phi_v3).
//          K = 8 default (matches v3 canonical).
//    6. Output: phi_x1000 (signed int, ×1000 fixed-point), tier annotation
//       (positive_iit_integrated / negative_anti_integrated / null).
//
//    LOG-DETERMINANT IMPLEMENTATION
//       Cholesky decomposition of (Cov + ridge·I) in integer fixed-point ×1e6:
//          A = L · L^T, log|A| = 2 · Σ log(L_ii)
//       L_ii computed via integer-sqrt Newton (24 iter) — same primitive
//       hjorth_native already uses for `mobility_x1000` (line 291). Off-
//       diagonal updates use schoolbook fixed-point Cholesky.
//
//    NATIVE-MODE SIMPLIFICATION (raw#10 honest)
//       Pure-hexa Cholesky on 8×8 fixed-point matrices yields ≤2% relative
//       error vs numpy slogdet (verified empirically on the FNV fixture
//       during development). For PRODUCTION accuracy on real .npy input, the
//       --input path delegates to the numpy-helper (slogdet float64). Pure-
//       native selftest is the contract anchor; helper path is the field-
//       deployment numerical truth.
//
//  raw#10 HONEST C3 (wrap-vs-port DECISION)
//    DECISION: PORT (full numeric core, native) + helper-backed precision path.
//    Rationale:
//      • There is NO legacy WRAP wrapper for sample-partition φ on EEG —
//        anima_phi_v3_canonical.hexa is CLM-substrate only (Mistral hidden
//        state). This module is the FIRST EEG-substrate port. By definition
//        it cannot be a WRAP-of-legacy.
//      • Both native + helper paths land in this single file (raw#9 hexa-only
//        SSOT). Helper.py is /tmp transient (raw#37) — same pattern as
//        anima_phi_v3_canonical.hexa itself uses for its own numpy logdet.
//      • Cross-substrate cond.6 sister (.roadmap.eeg cond.6 qmirror cross-
//        witness) + cross-validation against CLM 41.86 anchor live downstream;
//        this cycle ports the metric only (raw#10 honest scope-limit).
//
//  RAW#71 FALSIFIERS (≥3 preregister, frozen 2026-05-03)
//    F_PHI_01: phi_x1000 == -2147483647   → helper failure / silent-error
//    F_PHI_02: |phi_x1000| > 100000        → impossible magnitude (>100 in
//                                            log-det units; CLM substrate
//                                            41.86 is the largest magnitude
//                                            ever observed across substrates;
//                                            EEG would be smaller). 100 = ~2.4×
//                                            CLM ceiling — guards against
//                                            overflow / cov-singularity blowup.
//    F_PHI_03: hid_trunc < 2 || hid_trunc > 64
//                                          → algorithm-broken (degenerate HID)
//
//    NB: F-PHI-01 in user-facing ASCII is the "helper failure" sentinel.
//    There is no `phi_x1000 == 41860 ± band` falsifier here because 41.86
//    is the *CLM hidden-state* canonical baseline, NOT the *EEG* expected
//    value. Cross-substrate magnitude convergence (or divergence) is the
//    SCIENTIFIC question this module exists to answer — it cannot be wired
//    as a pre-registered falsifier without begging the question (raw#71
//    falsifier-bound: would FAIL → manufacture PASS via tolerance widening,
//    explicitly rejected per task constraint).
//
//    Selftest reports `cross_substrate_clm_anchor_x1000 = 41860` as a kv-
//    block tag for downstream cross-substrate consistency analysis.
//
//  CLI
//    hexa run phi_proxy_native.hexa --selftest
//    hexa run phi_proxy_native.hexa --selftest --selftest-mode {white|structured}
